2.67` under HALF_UP)\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: this changes how amounts ending exactly in a half cent are rounded at every place that calls `round_money`.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 379910, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012gbdbc6a1EzaqrJUvhNWXv", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379910, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012gbdbc6a1EzaqrJUvhNWXv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 4585137, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). For example, it rounded 2.665 to 2.67 when the test expects 2.66.\n- **The fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updated the import, on branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n**What reviewers should know:** this changes results anywhere `round_money` is used, but only for amounts that land exactly on half a cent.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212: the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. The required behaviour comes from the test and the function's own description, which agree with each other.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UdTY41c9fxSRtgN9YR99zU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YKH2L27SAh41Rizh9mGoyw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KpdR1uA3MW66kRyJnY8c7Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The fix is clear: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN, but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. Both test cases (2.675\u21922.68, 2.665\u21922.66) match half-even. Creating a branch:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01H6zbS2j8zeQStXKX96riRW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018xREnGdFh989rinJhoUiDh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JwKptNoAHyX7PgJVLuxFxZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013y6N36CjKjUBC5fn4y3K5J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the PR:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012gbdbc6a1EzaqrJUvhNWXv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build failed because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\n**Change:** `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. This is a one-line change plus the import.\n\n- `2.675` \u2192 `2.68` (no change)\n- `2.665` \u2192 `2.66` (was `2.67` under HALF_UP)\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: this changes how amounts ending exactly in a half cent are rounded at every place that calls `round_money`.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). For example, it rounded 2.665 to 2.67 when the test expects 2.66.\n- **The fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updated the import, on branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n**What reviewers should know:** this changes results anywhere `round_money` is used, but only for amounts that land exactly on half a cent.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212: the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. The required behaviour comes from the test and the function's own description, which agree with each other.", "type": "text"}]}]}